---
// /directory/terms/ — public listing terms of the GHS Tools & Services Directory (s110, 15.10.2026).
//
// Why it exists: a vendor (Every Software Solutions) asked for the conditions we state by e-mail — free listing,
// no contract, removal on request, optional badge and links, the right to withdraw logo and content — to be
// written down publicly before it considers claiming. Policy source: Sergej's decisions of 15.10.2026
// (vendor-requested removal is fine; a paid Sponsored placement is mentioned only as an optional possibility).
//
// ⚠ §2 says that no paid placement exists today. check:dist (dir-terms) fails if any entry has tier 'featured',
//   so this text cannot silently go stale.
// ⚠ §4 does not contradict the hub principle "Nothing is deleted": that principle is about tools that closed down.
import Layout from '../../../layouts/Layout.astro'

const title = 'Directory Listing Terms'
const description =
  'The terms that apply to every listing in the GHS Tools & Services Directory: free to list and to claim, no contract, removal on request, optional badge and links.'
const canonical = 'https://ghspictograms.com/directory/terms/'
const updated = '15 October 2026'
export const prerender = true

const H2 = "font-family: 'Space Grotesk', system-ui, sans-serif"
---

<Layout title={title} description={description} canonical={canonical}>
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-10">
    <nav class="text-sm text-gray-500 mb-6" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/" class="text-[#062A78] hover:underline">Home</a>
      <span class="mx-2">→</span>
      <a href="/directory/" class="text-[#062A78] hover:underline">Directory</a>
      <span class="mx-2">→</span>
      <span class="text-gray-700">Listing terms</span>
    </nav>

    <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold text-gray-900 tracking-tight" style={H2}>
      Directory listing terms
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed text-lg">
      These terms apply to every listing in the
      <a href="/directory/" class="text-[#062A78] font-semibold hover:underline">GHS Tools &amp; Services Directory</a>,
      claimed or not. They supplement the <a href="/terms/" class="text-[#062A78] font-semibold hover:underline">Terms of Service</a>
      of ghspictograms.com. The directory is run by SIA Basis Assets, Riga, Latvia.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-gray-500">Last updated: {updated}</p>

    <ul class="mt-6 grid gap-2 sm:grid-cols-2 text-gray-800">
      <li class="rounded-lg border border-gray-200 bg-white px-4 py-3"><strong>Free.</strong> Listing, claiming and keeping a claimed listing cost nothing.</li>
      <li class="rounded-lg border border-gray-200 bg-white px-4 py-3"><strong>No contract.</strong> No signature, no minimum period, no penalty.</li>
      <li class="rounded-lg border border-gray-200 bg-white px-4 py-3"><strong>Removal on request.</strong> At any time, claimed or not.</li>
      <li class="rounded-lg border border-gray-200 bg-white px-4 py-3"><strong>Your content is yours.</strong> Logo and text can be withdrawn at any time.</li>
      <li class="rounded-lg border border-gray-200 bg-white px-4 py-3 sm:col-span-2"><strong>Badge and links are optional.</strong> Nothing about a listing depends on them.</li>
    </ul>

    <div class="mt-10 space-y-8 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[#062A78] mb-3" style={H2}>1. What a listing is</h2>
        <p>
          A listing is a card of facts about a vendor’s product or service. Each fact comes from the vendor’s own public
          pages or an official register, with its source and the date we checked it. We do not rate, rank or score anyone.
          A card is marked “not verified by owner” until the vendor claims it.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[#062A78] mb-3" style={H2}>2. Cost</h2>
        <p>
          Listing, claiming and keeping a claimed listing are free: no fee, subscription, renewal or other payment is
          required, now or later. The order inside a section is never sold: verified listings come first, ordered by the date
          the owner last confirmed the facts, and any vendor can reach that by claiming for free. A paid placement may be
          offered one day; if so, it would be optional, would sit in a separate block marked Sponsored, would move nothing
          in the list and would have nothing to do with claiming. None exists today.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[#062A78] mb-3" style={H2}>3. No contract</h2>
        <p>
          Claiming is an exchange of e-mails from an address on the vendor’s own domain. It creates no contract: no
          signature, no minimum period, no penalty, nothing to cancel. The owner may stop at any time.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[#062A78] mb-3" style={H2}>4. Removal</h2>
        <p>
          A vendor may ask for its listing to be removed at any time, claimed or not, by writing to
          <a href="mailto:hello@ghspictograms.com" class="text-[#062A78] font-semibold hover:underline">hello@ghspictograms.com</a>
          from an address on its own domain. Within a few working days we remove the card and everything the owner supplied,
          and we do not list the vendor again unless it asks us to. The principle “Nothing is deleted” on the
          <a href="/directory/" class="text-[#062A78] font-semibold hover:underline">directory page</a> concerns tools that have
          closed down: they stay on record as closed. It does not override a vendor’s own request.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[#062A78] mb-3" style={H2}>5. Logo, description and other content from the owner</h2>
        <p>
          A logo, a short description and links appear only if the owner supplies them. The owner may withdraw any of them at
          any time by writing to the same address. We then take them off, together with anything on the card that rests only
          on the owner’s word, and the card returns to the sourced facts.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[#062A78] mb-3" style={H2}>6. Badge and links</h2>
        <p>
          The directory’s badges, such as “Verified listing”, are offered, never required. A vendor is not obliged to display
          a badge or to link to this site, and nothing about its listing depends on it.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[#062A78] mb-3" style={H2}>7. Corrections</h2>
        <p>
          If a fact on a card is wrong or out of date, write to
          <a href="mailto:hello@ghspictograms.com" class="text-[#062A78] font-semibold hover:underline">hello@ghspictograms.com</a>.
          We check it against the vendor’s page and correct it, usually within a few working days. Corrections are free.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[#062A78] mb-3" style={H2}>Contact</h2>
        <p>
          <a href="mailto:hello@ghspictograms.com" class="text-[#062A78] font-semibold hover:underline">hello@ghspictograms.com</a>
          · SIA Basis Assets, Riga, Latvia
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
